No idea.  I bought a heat sink kit on Ebay that included the new
insert the first time I needed one.  When I replaced the 166 in my
AS200 with a 275MHz from a Cabriolet (ran it at 233!) and removed the
fanned heat sink to use the stock tall aluminum one, I used a fine
polishing compound on glass to make the base of the heat sink as
smooth and flat as possible (and cleaned/degreased it and the top of
the Alpha with 1,1,1 trichloroethane from my stash), then used high
quality heat transfer grease (like the peecee overclockers use)
between it and the Alpha.  It has been running reliably for several
years.

I do NOT know if this would work adequately on the faster chip as I've
never had the need to disassemble one from its heat sink, but in lieue
of the correct grafoil insert, its probably the way you need to go. 
You can find usable heat transfer grease at Radio Shack, but the stuff
from peecee specialty places is supposed to be better at moving the
heat.

Good luck...

Rich


