> Do you know what differences exist between IOS 11.2(16) and IOS 11.1(6)?
> Does 11.2(16) have NAT?

Unfortunately IOS 11.2 has NAT only in its Plus-Versions.
Ihe IOS shipped with the DECbrouters had always the Enterprise-Feature
(J-L)
while you would need the Enterprise-Plus-Version (JS-L).
After I got 11.2(16) from DNPG I started a little search on the net
and found
some other versions including (C2500-JS-L), Version 11.2(4).
If you do not need the Enterprise-Features (DECnet, LAT, TN3270,
AppleTalk)
you could go up to 12.1(14) IP-Only (I-L) which I am running right now
(including NAT).
The Advantage in IP-Only-IOS lies in the reduced image-size
compared to Enterprise-IOS resulting in later releases fitting the
flash and
reduced licensing fees (there is no DEC-License for later versions)
and the IP-Only-License cost me only about 15 USD.

If you need any of the above please email me.


