I think he's referring to one of the whitebox Digital 3000 servers, not 
the old 3000-xxx Turbochannel series; the 3000 was the "NT only" 
equivalent of the Alphaserver 800.  21164A is an EV56 chip; I've not 
seen the markings on one of these but if the 'A' is normally marked on 
the chip, I'd have to assume the 21164-P7 is an EV5.

If its the newer Digital 3000 server, OpenVMS is not supported, but has 
been reported to run on that system if the current firmware is loaded 
and VMS compatible graphics adapter, SCSI adapter, and SCSI devices are 
installed.

Please note that if you pulled the heat sink to look at the Alpha chip 
to get the numbers, the graf-foil (sp?) insert should be replaced.  It 
is supposed to be a one-shot deal.

Rich Jordan

