I haven't used Steam agents for a long time. I tend to configure an HSG80
the old-fashioned way via direct CLI. As for error reporting, the SWMA
(SANWorks Management Appliance) is almost a must have. You can configure it
to send pager or mail on error, or to forward SNMP traps to whatever
management tools you use in your network.
The SWMA is the base for several applications, the HSG80 Element Manager
being one of them. Others incluse Enterprise Volume Manager, Allocation
Reporter, Network View.
