You've got a couple of choices to recover the data.

RainDOS- this driver from Sydex allows a PC with a high density 5.25"
drive to read MS-DOS formatted Rainbow disks.  The only problem is the
software cannot be run on fast PC's.   You'll need a 486/25MHz or
slower for it to work properly. 

22Disk - This program can read CP/M formatted Rainbow disks.  Again,
it is from Sydex.  Both this and RainDOS should be available on any
site with the Simtel archives.  

Serial Transfer - This might be the easiest if the user had any sort
of terminal program.  Just connect a null modem between the Rainbow
and a PC and transfer the files.  The Rainbow's serial port speeds can
be configured by pressing the "Setup" key and finiding the proper
screen for configuring the serial ports.  

Those are your best bets aside from anything overwhelmingly
complicated.  Hope I've helped!

