                      Fifteenth International
          Software and Internet Quality Week Conference,
            3-6 September 2002, San Francisco, CA  USA

QW2002 has always had the reputation of keeping its finger on the
community's technological pulse...and this year is no exception!

We're very proud to summarize the presentations from the great
lineup of keynoters we have for you this year!

  * Mr. Fred Baker (Cisco Systems): Internet Reliability Under
    Stress.

    We all know how critical the Internet has become...and you can
    bet that it will experience a lot of stress in coming months and
    years. Baker's talk will emphasize how Cisco aims to enhance
    reliability!

  * Mr. Greg Pope (LLNL): You Want It When?

    If you have ever had a problem getting the budget you need to do
    the work you're supposed to get done by yesterday -- of course!
    -- you'll not want to miss this!

  * Mr. Erik Simmons (Intel) The Human Side Of Risk.

    Software and WebSite development and deployment involve risk, of
    course!  But people are involved, too. How do you achieve
    balance? Hear this talk and learn!

  * Prof. Dick Hamlet (Portland State): Science, Computer "Science",
    Mathematics, and Software Development.

    And you thought software engineering and quality assurance was a
    scientific endeavor. Think again! A renowned speaker and a
    distinguished researcher tells it like it really is!

  * Mr. Don O'Neill (Center for National Software Studies):
    Competitiveness Versus Security.

    Do you want it reliable and fast or do you want it to be secure?
    In these difficult times this may be the question! From the
    newly started Center for National Software Studies, hear Don
    discusses the tradeoffs!  Then, make up your own minds!

  * Mr. Robert V. Binder (Mobile Systems Verification):  Achieving
    Very High Reliability for Ubiquitous Information Technology.

    In The Wired World everyone is wired in -- even if the last leg
    of the connection is "wireless" and mobile. You can bet people
    will grow to depend on these technologies -- just look at the
    cell-phone! -- but how can you really assure the reliability of
    such widespread networking? Bob Binder will tell you how!

Special Panel Sessions at QW2002 give us an opportunity to address
key issues from multiple perspectives.  We've lined up two special
Panel Sessions for QW2002.

  * Ross Collard (Consultant): The Value of Agile Testing.

    Is agile testing (the QA side of Extreme Programming) a good
    story, or is it bunko?  Consultant Ross Collard will bring
    competing voices to this sure-to-be raucous panel!

  * Selim Aissi (Intel): Web Services, QoS, Reliability and
    Security.

    In the increasingly Wired World the quality of what users
    receive (and what you send them) becomes more and more
    important.  But how do you measure "quality" and what does it
    really mean?  Everyone wants better quality. But how do you get
    it?  The panelists will take on this tough question from every
    side! Don't miss this one!

Complete QW2002 conference content and a convenient on-line
registration form are available at <http://www.qualityweek.com>.

