And if a serial console is set up, what is NOT logged is equally important. If
there is absolutely no message on the console between the last opcom message
and the reboot sequence, then you can also conclude stuff.

And if the system performs the self tests that are seen after power-up, then
you can conclude power problems, whereas if the system just reboots in away
similar to the auto-reboot after a crash, the reasons would be more fuzzy.


