>Is this still supported / sold for the vax, and if so is it available under
>a hobbyist license.

Digital UNIX was the name of the UNIX operating system for Alpha
systems after it was changed from DEC OSF/1.  After the Compaq/
Digital merger it was called Tru64 UNIX.  It continues to be sold
for Alpha systems.  It was never available on VAX systems or MIPS
systems.

If you really meant VAX/ULTRIX, I think it stopped being supported
on or around December 31st, 2000 along with the MIPS version.  We
probably don't have it in a price list anymore.  Even if you could
get a media kit generated from the archives, you probably wouldn't
want to afford it.  You might find someone with media to sell, but
licenses could be a problem; not legally transferable and necessary
for more than a 2 user system.  The set of systems supported by the
VAX kit is also more limited than what OpenVMS supports.

