Dan Williams wrote:
>
> I have three vaxstations, one running vms and one running netbsd. I wanted
> one running ultrix, an article I was reading said the ultrix became digital
> unix. I just assumed it still run on the vax. So is ultrix still used on
> systems and sold.

Ultrix was DEC's version of Unix back when VAX was still alive and
breathing. It also ran on MIPS based DECstations. It's the common
Unix for both platforms.
Alphas were only sold with OSF1/DEC Unix/Tru64. That makes some
people think that it's just a renamed Ultrix, but it's essentially
a different beast. Early OSF1 versions just looked very much like
Ultrix.
Personally I really like Ultrix. It's a very nice system that works
stable and it's pretty fast too. There are still some people out
there using Ultrix. It's pretty GNU compatible too. You can get
much more software to compile on Ultrix than on any other vintage
Unix system (well, maybe except SunOS).
As you just say that you have "VAXstations" you might get some
problems. Ultrix does not support the later VAX models, so if
