Like many of the newer Alphas, the DS10 has 5V available even when the 
power is "off".  It only goes away if the line cord is unplugged, so an 
environmental failure, such as a real or imagined fan failure, should 
leave an amber led lit on the console.  That not being the case in this 
situation, one would suspect the unit either actually lost wall power or 
the power supply has an intermittent problem or bad connection either 
internally or to the outside world.  I would pull the supply and put it 
back in if no maintenance contract or warranty was in place.  Otherwise, 
just log a service call and ask that the power supply be replaced.

