"Gerry Hooper" <gritineye@bikerider.com> wrote in message news:<afptc7$g9a2u$1@ID-14595.news.dfncis.de>...
> Hi,
> 
> We've got a LA400 and have misplaced the manual. Can anyone advice how 
> you switch between Draft and Letter Quality by using the front panel 
> switches? 

I don't know how many models there were in the LA400 series or how
they differ, but FWIW, from the LA_424_ manual:-

Switch on the printer, then press Setup.
Press Down Arrow several times until you reach Density.
Press Right Arrow until you get Letter Quality.
Press Select.
Press Down Arrow until you get DEC Defaults.
Press Right Arrow once to get Save.
Press Select to save the new setup and return to on-line mode.

This assumes you want DEC mode. For "Emulation" mode, select it using
the Right Arrow button at the Protocol level. Then proceed as above;
Letter Quality is selected from the Typestyle sub-menu.

For those who wonder about the precise wording of the first step above
-- there's a whole new setup menu (serial port baud rate etc.)
obtained by holding down setup while you switch on.

Chris


